    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26972" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longŭlus</span></b> , a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. dim.</i>
			[longus], <i>rather long</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 16, 13</span></i>
			, a.— Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longŭlē</span></b> , <i>rather far</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haud longule ex hoc loco,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Rud. 1, 5, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Men. prol. 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Heaut.
				2, 2, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p.
			224</span></i>.</div>
